---
import ArticleLayout from "../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro";
import Prose from "../components/article/Prose.astro";
import LinkCard from "../components/article/LinkCard.astro";
---

<ArticleLayout
  title="Workflow Guides - Summit AI Notes"
  description="Step-by-step workflows for recording, reviewing, searching, and exporting meeting notes in Summit."
  breadcrumb={[{ name: "Guides" }]}
  heading="Workflow guides"
  lead="Follow a meeting from recording to a useful, searchable record."
>
  <Prose>
    <h2>Your first meeting</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><a href="/docs/setup/getting-started">Set up audio, speech recognition, and AI summaries</a>.</li>
      <li><a href="/docs/guides/recording">Record a call or import an audio or video file</a>.</li>
      <li><a href="/docs/guides/transcription">Review the transcript, name speakers, and check important details</a>.</li>
      <li><a href="/docs/guides/summary-templates">Choose a summary template</a> for the meeting's purpose.</li>
      <li><a href="/docs/guides/export">Export the result</a> to your notes app or share selected content.</li>
    </ol>
    <h2>A day of back-to-back calls</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="/docs/guides/calendar">Connect your calendar</a> and choose which events to record.
      Use <a href="/docs/setup/local-ai#decide-when-your-mac-should-process">deferred processing</a> to leave resources available during calls.
      If one recording spans several meetings, <a href="/docs/guides/split-recordings">split it into notes</a> before generating their summaries.
    </p>
    <h2>Follow up on a project</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="/docs/guides/organization">Group notes into folders and tags</a>.
      <a href="/docs/guides/search">Search for a decision and open the matching passage</a>, then
      <a href="/docs/guides/chat">ask a scoped question across the project</a>.
      Review the cited notes before sharing a conclusion.
    </p>
    <h2>Capture away from your Mac</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="/docs/guides/icloud-sync">Record with the iPhone companion and sync to the Mac for processing</a>.
      Keep your recovery phrase available for the encryption setup on each device.
    </p>
    <h2>Use your notes in other tools</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="/docs/guides/export">Set up automatic Markdown export</a> for a local knowledge base,
      or <a href="/docs/guides/mcp-server">connect an MCP client</a> to query meetings.
      The receiving app's storage and AI settings determine what happens to exported or retrieved content.
    </p>
  </Prose>
  <LinkCard slot="after-card" href="/docs" kicker="Reference" title="Browse all documentation" />
  <LinkCard slot="after-card" href="/docs/guides/troubleshooting" kicker="Help" title="Troubleshoot a problem" align="right" />
</ArticleLayout>
